SWEET AOC firmware load (patch 0164, plan 2026-11-14 oneshot-2 step A6), boot-arg sweetaoc=2 (sweetaoc=1 stays the A4 read probe).
The stock aoc.bin (15,158,976 B, sha256 9be56622...5743, docs/research/50) arrives zlib-compressed as /chosen/memory-map AOCFW
(tools/pack_aocfw.py, tools/mkpayload.py --aocfw, xrun/build-xnu-image.sh --aocfw). Order (row A6 = aoc_fw_callback, aoc.c:472-674):
inflate + length/sha256 against the pinned identity with no hardware access; PMU AOC_STATUS bit 0 must be 1; aoc_req 0x175D0000 := 1;
_aoc_fw_is_valid/_aoc_fw_is_signed header checks; header (4096 B) into a wired page, body to the carveout 0x94000000 (bounded by
0x03000000); read back and sha256 again; GSA mailbox 0x17C90000 GSA_MB_CMD_LOAD_AOC_FW_IMG (90), argc 4 (header PA, 0x94000000),
the stock exec_mbox_cmd_sync_locked register sequence with a 10 s bounded poll; expect err 0. No other GSA command, no AOC start
(A8), no retry. Pure logic in bsd/dev/sweet_aoc_load.h (host test shim/aoc_load_host_test.c). Pass line "SWEET AOC: gsa load ok".
Without sweetaoc=2 nothing changes.
Round 2 (after run o6-a6-aocload stopped silently right after "pass 2"): round 1 mapped all 48 MiB of the carveout with
ml_io_map_wcomb, which allocates KMA_NOFAIL from io_submap, only 8 MiB (IO_MAP_SIZE, osfmk/arm/io_map.c:65, :120-130): a
kmem_alloc panic before the first carveout byte. Now only the body extent is mapped, through ml_io_map_unmappable (kernel_map),
one word is written and read back first, the copy prints a line per MiB, and the mapping is removed before the GSA call.

